# AHS full-muguet inventory and architecture audit — 2026-09-07

## Decision and evidence boundary

The user reports actually adding Florol 240 µL and Nympheal 60 µL, and still finds fullness insufficient. This is accepted as uncontrolled sensory evidence. It does not identify masking, a missing molecule, or a required dose. The next design is a **body-led full-heart bench candidate**, not a commercial-formula reconstruction or released whole-bottle rescue.

All live inventory categories were read. Inventory SHA-256: d103b79508592f74bb368f27507874b9fd3493acc9e872150e768449b2a02ef7. Historic family guidance and catalog ownership flags were checked against the actual stock lines. The named product and fraction basis are preserved; “as supplied” is not an analytical purity declaration.

## Direct muguet/cyclamen/freesia palette

| Material | Live stock | Accord role to evaluate | Current decision |
|---|---|---|---|
| Florol | As supplied | Soft fresh muguet body | Already added; retain, do not repeat |
| Nympheal | As supplied | Watery-green floral density/definition | Already added; retain, do not repeat |
| Helional | Neat plus separate 10% v/v stock, diluted carrier unstated | Green/cyclamen watery connection | Existing neat dose retained; do not use the diluted stock interchangeably |
| Lilyreal ND | HAVE — supplied product, composition not inferred; SKU 6MG22777 | Sustained soft lily/cyclamen body | Selected main new body hypothesis; opaque blend OAV cannot be represented exactly |
| Bourgeonal | 20% in TEC; fraction basis unspecified | Muguet aldehydic definition and woody depth | Excluded from this dose; stock/physics/safety gaps require adjudication |
| Mayol | As supplied | Transparent muguet-lily freshness | Alternative; no distinct missing role established after Florol/Nympheal |
