## Supporting palette — not interchangeable muguet cores

| Plane | Inventory candidates | Selection and boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Mild petal texture | Hydroxycitronellol neat | Selected smaller soft rose-peony modifier, **not Hydroxycitronellal**, not a promised high-impact booster |
| Floral blending/body | Phenethyl Alcohol, PEDMC, DBCA, Peonile | PEA selected at smaller share for rose-petal blending; others remain alternatives because they can introduce magnolia/gardenia/peony character |
| Rosy/citrus-floral detail | Geraniol neat and 10% DPG; Citronellol; Nerol; Rhodinol ex Citronella; Geranium EO/Flower EO; rose EO; Rose de Mai 10% DPG | Existing Geranium preserved; no extra rose-led character added by default. PEA is not a dose-equivalent substitute for these |
| Floral air and continuity | Hedione; Linalool; Linalyl Acetate; Neroli EO neat; Petitgrain EO Paraguay | Already present and retained; no additional “radiance” dose by reflex |
| Waxy/lily texture | Farnesol; ACA; Nerolidol | Considered, not selected. Existing complaint does not establish need for more wax or fixation; ACA is jasmine-muguet, not neutral body |
| Salicylate foundation | Benzyl Salicylate; Hexyl Salicylate | Benzyl Salicylate already 250 µL; no more fixation by default |
| Green salicylate continuity | cis-3-Hexenyl Salicylate 20% w/w | Owned, carrier unspecified, explicit quantitative dosing HOLD; not selected |
| Leaf-flower detail | cis-3-Hexenol 1%; Undecavertol 1%; Verdyl Acetate; Liffarome 10% w/w; PADMA; Stralyl Acetate | Not selected for body; Liffarome carrier unresolved/HOLD. PADMA is phenylacetaldehyde dimethyl acetal, **not** Hydroxycitronellal dimethyl acetal |
| Stronger leaf/green contour | Parmavert; Leafovert neat; Triplal; Dynascone 10%; Violet Leaf Absolute 10% DPG; Tagetes EO 10% DPG | Alternate character directions, not muguet fullness defaults. Galbanum is out of stock |
| Watery/ozonic modifiers | Adoxal 10% DPG; Floralozone 10%; Scentenal 1%; Melonal; Calone 1% | Existing Calone retained. Additional ozone/melon does not establish fuller petals |
| Jasmine/orange-flower elaboration | Benzyl Acetate; Jasmine Absolute 10% DPG; Jasmine Sambac 10% DPG; Dihydrojasmone; Jessemal; Cis Jasmone; Indole10%; Ylang grades; Aurantiol neat; Methyl Anthranilate | Available elaborations, not necessary members of this AHS-adjacent muguet correction; preserve the fresh woody/citrus target |
| Non-core foundation | Existing musks, woods, methylionone and carriers | Already represented; increasing count is not proof of depth |

Paradisamide is tropical-fruity, not a missing muguet core. No new fruit, spice, gourmand, resin, earth or animalic layer is justified by the current fullness report.

**Not listed as current inventory:** Hydroxycitronellal, Hydroxycitronellal dimethyl acetal, Lilyflore, Lilybelle, Mahonial, Florhydral, Florosa, Hivernal and Lyral. Hydroxycitronellal is also depleted in H.yaml. Absence is not a purchasing instruction. Old family guidance claiming it is buildable must not override stock truth.

## Full accord architecture in the treated perfume

1. **Fresh muguet definition:** retain Florol/Nympheal/Helional; no repeated transfers.
2. **Sustained floral body:** introduce Lilyreal ND as the named supplied blend, not a fictitious single molecule.
3. **Soft petal texture:** a smaller Hydroxycitronellol hypothesis; its mildness and rosy identity are explicit.
4. **Floral blending:** a smaller PEA hypothesis, checked against rose drift.
5. **Leaf/citrus-to-flower connection:** existing Linalool/Linalyl Acetate, Geranium, Petitgrain and Neroli.
6. **Floral-to-drydown connection:** existing Hedione, Benzyl Salicylate, methylionone, woods and musks.

The new draft ratio is **6:2:1 supplied-stock volume** (Lilyreal ND : Hydroxycitronellol : PEA). It is an exploratory hypothesis, not a mass ratio, validated optimum or perceived contribution. The complete accord comprises new and existing materials; it does not require every material in the inventory.

The isolated candidate is documented in [the addition card](../../formulas/AHS_MuguetFullHeart_AddOnly_CARD_20260907.md) and the [complete recipe](../../formulas/AHS_UserBottle_MuguetFullHeart_20260907.md). No new physical addition is claimed.

## Primary-source check

- [PerfumersWorld Lilyreal ND, SKU 6MG22777](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=6MG22777): named mixture, soft lily/cyclamen and hydroxycitronellal-like description. Replacement positioning is not identity equivalence or disclosure of ingredients. Supplier tenacity is not measured performance in this bottle.
- [PerfumersWorld PEA, SKU 3RM00358](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=3RM00358): soft rose description and muguet/floral-blender uses. This supports the role, not the dose.
- [NHU Hydroxycitronellol specification](https://www.nhu-eu.com/pic/upload/NHU-EUROPE-GmbH---1.1.3.25---Hydroxycitronellol---11-2025---Specification-9.00.0002-NHU-24-00096.pdf): search-indexed primary text dated 2025-11-28 identifies CAS107-74-4, MW174.28 and soft-rose odor. Direct PDF fetch failed; no complete document/lot validation is claimed.
- [Api et al., RIFM Hydroxycitronellol assessment](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38049060/): identity CAS107-74-4, Food Chem Toxicol183(2024)114281. Individual ingredient assessment is not finished-formula approval.
- [PerfumersWorld Bourgeonal](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=4MA00067) and [supplier SDS](https://www.perfumersworld.com/document-list.php?pro_id=4MA00067): muguet/woody role; SDS CAS18127-01-0 and MW190.29, versus local MW176.25. SDS includes H361 and irritation/sensitization concerns. No current 20% TEC mixture clearance is inferred.
- [EU Regulation2021/1902](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32021R1902): Lilial/butylphenyl methylpropional CAS80-54-6 added to prohibited cosmetic ingredients. This is an EU boundary, not an invented global legal claim.
- [Florol manufacturer](https://studio.dsm-firmenich.com/product/florolr-pe-966458) and [Nympheal manufacturer](https://www.givaudan.com/fragrance-beauty/fragrance-ingredients-business/fragrance-molecules/nympheal) role evidence retained from the preceding design; no proprietary Chanel ratios inferred.

## Quantitative and scientific limitations

Lilyreal ND has no disclosed constituent map or measured whole-product ODT in this record. Its local MW192.3/VP0.01 and ODT2ppb are not an accepted physical representation of the mixture. Hydroxycitronellol air ODT100ppb is an explicit derived class proxy, not a measured threshold. PEA air ODT26ppb is literature-tagged, but matrix headspace and masking remain unmeasured. Florol's existing MW conflict persists. Bourgeonal's local stock1.0 contradicts owned20%TEC and its verification metadata incorrectly describes a whole oil.

No active mass, exact concentrate ppm w/w, percentage muguet contribution, real-world punch or safety conclusion is manufactured from these numbers. A focused pipeline diagnostic can expose the gaps but cannot certify the accord. No source/config/model values are changed for this design.

## Verification scope and next acceptance

The new user-report checkpoint preserves the complete29-row parent and records the actual F240/N60 report without forging a measured engine event. The next candidate adds only three rows and preserves every previous dose/stock. Parent-linked guard and parser checks are separate from sensory acceptance. Full module versus Lilyreal-only and individual omission comparisons are needed to establish whether the extra mild materials earn their place. Define matching vehicle before claiming carrier-matched controls; none has been executed.

This is research + design + diagnostic work, not a release. Safety/release remain HOLD; current remainder, stability, controlled fullness improvement and reference similarity are unresolved. No inventory rewrite, recipe-history rewrite, core code change, Git integration or push is part of this task.
